## Streaming API — sendMessageDraft + sendRichMessageDraft

The two streaming methods that make Telegram a real AI interface.

---

## sendMessageDraft (plain text streaming)
30-second ephemeral preview. Must call sendMessage to persist. Returns True.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer | Yes | Target private chat |
| message_thread_id | Integer | Optional | Thread |
| draft_id | Integer | Yes | Non-zero. Same ID = animated transitions |
| text | String | Optional | 0-4096 chars. Empty = "Thinking..." placeholder |
| parse_mode | String | Optional | HTML/Markdown |
| entities | Array of MessageEntity | Optional | Custom entities |

## sendRichMessageDraft (block streaming)
30-second ephemeral preview. Must call sendRichMessage to persist. Returns True.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| chat_id | Integer | Yes | Target private chat |
| message_thread_id | Integer | Optional | Thread |
| draft_id | Integer | Yes | Non-zero. Same ID = animated transitions |
| rich_message | InputRichMessage | Yes | Partial message. No direct file upload. |

---

## Behavior

- Draft is EPHEMERAL — disappears after 30 seconds of no updates
- Same draft_id = transitions are ANIMATED (smooth token streaming)
- Different draft_id = new draft replaces old
- Empty text in sendMessageDraft = "Thinking..." placeholder
- InputRichBlockThinking = rich version of "Thinking..." (draft only, cannot persist)
- Must call sendMessage / sendRichMessage with final content to persist
- Private chats only (chat_id is Integer, not String)
- No direct file upload in draft — use file_id references

---

## Implementation pattern for TPR

### Simple text streaming (current TPR baseline)
```
1. Receive update → extract chat_id, message_thread_id
2. Start inference (Qwen-max / ORION)
3. As tokens arrive in chunks:
     POST sendMessageDraft { chat_id, draft_id: 1, text: accumulated_text }
4. On completion:
     POST sendMessage { chat_id, text: final_text, message_thread_id }
```

### Rich message streaming (full agent mode)
```
1. Receive update → extract chat_id, message_thread_id
2. Start inference
3. While generating:
     POST sendRichMessageDraft {
       chat_id, draft_id: 1,
       rich_message: {
         blocks: [
           { type: "thinking", text: "Reasoning..." },
           { type: "paragraph", text: partial_output }
         ]
       }
     }
4. On tool call:
     POST sendRichMessageDraft {
       chat_id, draft_id: 1,
       rich_message: {
         blocks: [
           { type: "details", summary: "Running: read_file", blocks: [...] },
           { type: "paragraph", text: "Reading file..." }
         ]
       }
     }
5. On completion:
     POST sendRichMessage {
       chat_id, message_thread_id,
       rich_message: {
         blocks: [
           { type: "paragraph", text: "Here's what I found:" },
           { type: "pre", text: code_output, language: "python" },
           { type: "paragraph", text: explanation }
         ]
       }
     }
```

### Timing considerations
- 30s timeout = must send updates at least every 30s during long operations
- For tool calls that take >30s: send a progress draft every ~20s
- draft_id should be unique per "turn" — increment per user message
- Animated transitions = smooth UX when same draft_id is reused

---

## Limits (observed, not all officially documented)
- text: 0-4096 characters per draft
- draft TTL: 30 seconds from last update
- Private chats only for drafts
- No file upload in drafts (use file_id from previous uploads)
- chat_id must be Integer (not @username string)

:: ∎
